	<ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="tb-00" contextRef="c-00">
&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Description of Business&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;Portland Natural Gas Transmission System ("PNGTS", "the Company", or "Acquiree") owns a 296-mile natural gas pipeline, which includes 107 miles of jointly owned pipeline facilities ("the Joint Facilities") with Maritimes and Northeast Pipeline L.L.C. ("MNE"), extending from United States-Canadian border near Pittsburg, New Hampshire to Dracut, Massachusetts. The Joint Facilities extend from Westbrook, Maine to Dracut, Massachusetts and the Company owns 52.5 percent of the undivided ownership interest based on contractually agreed upon percentages. M&amp;amp;N Operating Company, LLC ("M&amp;amp;N"), a subsidiary of MNE, operates and maintains the Joint Facilities on behalf of the joint ownership and PNGTS reimburses MNE for operating costs related to its share of the Joint Facilities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;On August 15, 2024, TC Energy Corporation ("TC Energy") and its joint venture partner, Energir Inc. ("Energir"), sold their entire interest in the Company to Beehive Loop AcquisitionCo LLC ("Beehive", "Parent", or "Acquirer"), which holds a 99.99% ownership interest of PNGTS ("Acquisition", "Acquisition Transaction"). The remainder 0.01% is owned by the wholly owned subsidiary Beehive Loop StubCo LLC. As a result of the Acquisition, the Company's structure was changed from a partnership to a disregarded entity and the partners' equity was converted to members' equity within the Statement of Equity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;Subsequent to August 15, 2024, TransCanada Northern Border Inc. ("Northern Border-OpCo"), a wholly owned indirect subsidiary of TC Energy, continued to provide services in line with the Transition Service Agreement ("TSA") and continued to be the operator of PNGTS through April 2025. At the end of the TSA, TC Energy is no longer the operator of PNGTS.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;Prior to the Acquisition, PNGTS was a joint venture between TC PipeLines, L.P. ("TCP") (61.71 percent) and Northern New England Investment Company ("NNEIC") (38.29 percent). TCP is an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of TC Energy. NNEIC is a subsidiary of Energir.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared in conformity with the accounting practices prescribed by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than the U.S. generally accep ted accounting principles (USGAAP). The most significant differences between USGAAP and the financial statements presented herein are the inclusion of a federal income tax provision, as well as classifications of certain accounts on the balance sheets, statements of income, and statements of cash flows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;These unaudited financial statements have been prepared in accordance with interim period reporting requirements. Because this is an interim period presented using a condensed format, this report should be read along with the Company's 2025 Annual FERC Form No. 2 audited financial statements which include a summary of its significant accounting policies and other disclosures. The Company has made all adjustments that are of a normal, recurring nature to fairly present its interim period results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Commitments, Contingencies, Legal Proceedings, Environmental and Regulatory Matters&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;a.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Contingencies, Legal Proceedings, and Environmental Matters&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 36pt;"&gt;PNGTS is subject to various legal proceedings in the ordinary course of business. The accounting for contingencies covers a variety of business activities, including contingencies for legal and environmental liabilities. The Company accrues for these contingencies when the assessments indicate that it is probable that a liability has been incurred or an asset will not be recovered, and an amount can be reasonably estimated in accordance with ASC 450, &lt;i&gt;Contingencies&lt;/i&gt; (ASC 450). The Company bases these estimates on currently available facts and the estimates of the ultimate outcomes or resolution. Actual results may vary from estimates resulting in an impact, positive or negative, on results of operations and cash flows. The Company is not aware of any material contingent liabilities, including legal proceedings, nor any environmental matters that would have an effect on PNGTS's financial condition, results of operations, or cash flows as of March 31, 2026.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;b.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Regulatory Matters&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 36pt;"&gt;The FERC regulates the rates and charges for transportation of natural gas in interstate commerce. Natural gas companies may not charge rates that have been determined to be unjust and unreasonable by the FERC. Generally, the rates for interstate pipelines are based on the cost of service, including recovery of and a return on the pipeline's actual prudent historical cost investment. The rates and terms and conditions for service are found in each pipeline's FERC-approved tariff. Under its tariff, an interstate pipeline is allowed to charge for its services on the basis of stated transportation rates. Transportation rates are established periodically in FERC proceedings known as rate cases. The tariff also allows the interstate pipeline to provide services under negotiated and discounted rates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 36pt;"&gt;PNGTS continues to operate under the rates approved by FERC in the Company's last rate proceeding, effective December 1, 2010. The Company has no requirement to file a new rate proceeding.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size: 10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Leases&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 18pt;"&gt;PNGTS accounts for leases in accordance with Docket No AI19-1-000 which permits the Company to record operating leases that may be capitalized under USGAAP in the FERC balance sheet accounts that have already been established for capital lease assets and liabilities. Docket No AI19-1000 did not impact any existing ratemaking treatment or practices and all other provisions of regulatory lease accounting are not affected. The amounts included in the balance sheet accounts that relate to operating leases at June 30, 2026 are as follows:&lt;/p&gt;

